# Rust
backend/target
target

# Rust build artifacts (any crate)
**/target/

# Claude Code session state (local only)
.claude/

# Local environment files. backend/src/main.rs:69 calls dotenvy::dotenv(), so a
# developer's own .env is loaded at runtime and will hold real values for
# JWT_SECRET, GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY and the OAuth client
# secrets. There was NO rule here at all, so such a file showed as untracked
# and committable in a public repo.
#
# Prefix-matched, not exact: a rule matching only `.env` protects nothing once
# a suffix is appended (.env.bak, .env.local, .env.production) — that exact gap
# was found across five sibling repos.
#
# The two tracked TEMPLATES are kept deliberately: .env.example (URLs only) and
# .env.docker (docker-compose defaults). Neither is excluded here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.docker
